          "claim": "The quotient by the monic polynomial $X^2$ is the free abelian group with basis $1,X$. The displayed multiplication is the quotient-ring multiplication, so it is associative, commutative, and has unit $1$. On this basis, $\\epsilon$ and $\\Delta$ satisfy both counit identities; explicitly, $(\\epsilon\\otimes\\mathrm{id})\\Delta(1)=1$, $(\\mathrm{id}\\otimes\\epsilon)\\Delta(1)=1$, and the same composites send $X$ to $X$.",
