      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1.1",
          "claim": "If an edge does not meet the basepoint circle, its map is the identity on the basepoint factor and hence commutes with $X_p$. If the edge merges the basepoint circle with another circle, associativity gives $m(Xa\\otimes b)=X\\,m(a\\otimes b)$. If it splits the basepoint circle, the Frobenius identity gives $\\Delta(Xa)=(X\\otimes1)\\Delta(a)=(1\\otimes X)\\Delta(a)$; on $a=1,X$ these are respectively $X\\otimes X$ and $0$ on all three sides. Thus every edge map commutes with $X_p$, so $\\operatorname{im}(X_p)$ is a subcomplex.",
